---
source: crates/engram-cli/tests/cli/snapshot/help.rs
expression: "f.run_bare(& [\"stats\", \"--help\"])"
---
$ engramdb stats --help
exit: 0
--- stdout ---
Show statistics

Usage: engramdb stats [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --all-projects
          Include the cross-project telemetry breakdown

      --global
          Show statistics for the global (cross-project) memory store instead of the current project

      --daemon
          Show the shared embedding daemon's metrics instead of memory-store stats

      --memory <ID>
          Show one memory's usage (returned / injected / fetched, writes, last 30 days) instead of store stats. Accepts a unique id prefix

      --top <N>
          Append the N most-used memories (N >= 1)

      --by <BY>
          Which read signal orders --top; the others break ties (they are never summed)

          Possible values:
          - fetched:  Opened explicitly by id (`get`)
          - injected: Rendered into an agent's context by a hook
          - returned: Returned by a `query`
          
          [default: fetched]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - pretty: Human-friendly colored output with formatting
          - json:   JSON output for programmatic parsing
          - plain:  Plain text output without colors

      --json
          Output as JSON

  -q, --quiet
          Suppress non-essential output

  -v, --verbose
          Verbose output

      --no-color
          No colored output

      --dir <DIR>
          Working directory (default: current directory)

      --embedding-backend <EMBEDDING_BACKEND>
          Embedding backend: auto, onnx, or ollama

      --in-process
          Force in-process model loading — never contact the shared embedding daemon. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_IN_PROCESS=1

      --spawn-daemon
          Spawn the shared embedding daemon if it is not already running, then route through it. By default the CLI only uses a daemon that is already running (connect-only)

      --no-maintenance
          Skip the automatic main-worktree maintenance pass (orphan-project cleanup + a quick store health check) for this invocation. Equivalent to setting ENGRAMDB_DISABLE_AUTO_MAINTENANCE=1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
--- stderr ---
